fact WorkItem(id: "WI-269", description: some(value: "Implement proposal 042 — explicit type parameters on operations (docs/proposals/042-explicit-type-parameters-on-operations.md). Adds both the declaration-site form `operation foo[A, B](...) -> ...` and the call-site form `foo[A = Int, B = String](args)` / `foo[Int, String](args)` (positional + named, positional-first, same rule as SortBinding kernel spec §5.1). Replaces the WI-260 workaround in `stdlib/anthill/reflect/reflect.anthill:159` (`operation term_as_entity(t: Term) -> Option[T = ?E]` → `operation term_as_entity[E](t: Term) -> Option[E]`) and unblocks adding HOFs (`map`, `for_each`, `fold`) to `stdlib/anthill/prelude/{list,collection,iteration}.anthill` — currently these cannot be expressed because there is no surface to declare per-operation type parameters or bind them at the call site. Six-phase plan: (A) tree-sitter grammar — extend `operation_declaration` with optional `operation_type_param_list`; add `operation_type_arg_list` and allow `Name[bindings](args)` form before a `(` (instantiation_term + call disambiguates on next token vs proposal 035 sort-companion `.method`). (B) parse/ir.rs + parse/convert.rs — add `type_params: Vec<TypeParam>` to `Operation` (mirrors SortBinding for symmetry with 035); thread bindings table through call/Apply term. (C) kb/load.rs::load_operation — allocate a fresh `VarId` per declared type-param entry, bind name in operation`s local symbol scope before processing params / return / requires / ensures / effects; implicit `?T` mentions whose name matches a declared parameter resolve to the same var (round-trip with desugared form). (D) kb/typing.rs — at call-site `op[bindings](args)`, seed unification env from explicit bindings then run HM inference for remaining slots; diagnose explicit/inferred conflicts and unresolved parameters with a \"use op[T = ...]\" suggestion. (E) eval/{eval,value}.rs — populate `frame.requirements` with type-argument entries (positional, declaration order) AFTER sort-level entries per docs/design/operation-call-model.md §\"Operation type arguments\"; `apply_within` gains a `type_args` channel; closures capture both channels via the existing requirements-map mechanism. (F) stdlib + spec + tests — rewrite `reflect.term_as_entity` to the explicit form (WI-260 tests pass unchanged); add fixtures: `term_as_entity[WorkItem](t)` pins E to WorkItem; `operation foo[A, B](x: A, y: B) -> Pair[A = A, B = B]` parses + loads + type-checks; `map[A, B, C, E]` exercises both inferred and explicit calls (incl. effectful f propagating E); negative fixture for unconstrained `?E` with no context; frame-inspection fixture for `foo[T](x: T) -> T` per design doc; update `docs/kernel-language.md` §5.4 with the new Operation production + a §5.2 cross-reference. Out of scope (separate follow-up WIs): higher-rank `[F](f: F[A] -> F[B])`, declaration-site bounds `[T: Ordered]`, first-class operations, the actual HOF additions to `stdlib/anthill/prelude/list.anthill` etc. (filed separately once 042 lands). Acceptance: cargo-test green across the workspace; simplify clean on the changed Rust files; the proposal Acceptance bullets (foo[A,B] / term_as_entity[E] / map[A,B,C] fixtures + frame-inspection test) all pass."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-19T05:51:05Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-269", author: "user", content: "Phases A-D and Phase F (typing-only) delivered. Phase A (tree-sitter grammar) in 40f96dc, Phase B (parse IR + converter) in 3e0e88a, Phase C (loader registers op type-params as scoped) in b55cd42, Phase D (typer seeds substitution from explicit bindings) in 02528a8, Phase D follow-up (WI-270 typer top-down expected + diagnostic) in 8a70608. Phase F: spec §5.4 updated with operation_type_param_list grammar + §5.2 cross-reference (commit 4c87d32); typing-only acceptance fixtures added — foo[A,B](a:A,b:B) -> Pair[A=A,B=B] parses+loads+typechecks, map[A,B] type-checks both with explicit [A=Int,B=String] and inferred bindings, term_as_entity[E] pinned via let annotation or via explicit [E = Item] binding, negative case for unconstrained ?E surfaces the WI-270 diagnostic; stdlib reflect.term_as_entity rewritten to the explicit form (WI-260 tests pass unchanged). DEFERRED: Phase E (eval threading op type-args through frame.requirements per docs/design/operation-call-model.md §'Operation type arguments') — requires apply_within to gain a type_args positional channel, Frame.requirements (or a new Frame.type_args field) to hold (T_i, type_value) entries AFTER sort-level entries, closures to capture both channels via the existing requirements-map mechanism, and the frame-inspection acceptance fixture foo[T](x:T) -> T showing the T entry. Currently eval.rs ignores Expr::Apply.type_args (type_args: _). Filing as a follow-up. Acceptance bullets: foo[A,B] (✓), term_as_entity[E] (✓), map[A,B,C] (✓), frame-inspection (deferred to follow-up).", at: "2026-05-19T05:50:42Z")
